{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>The entire tribe of Levi.</b> Whether unblemished or whether blemished (Sifrei)." "<b>Portion.</b> In the spoil." "<b>And inheritance.</b> In the land (ibid.)." "<b>The fire-offerings of YHWH.</b> The consecrated gifts of the Sanctuary." "<b>And his inheritance.</b> These are the consecrated gifts of the boundary — terumot and ma'aserot; but a full inheritance <b>he shall not have among his brothers.</b> And in the Sifrei they expounded: <b>And inheritance he shall not have</b> — this is the inheritance of the remainder; <b>among his brothers</b> — this is the inheritance of five. And I do not know what it is, and it appears to me that the land of Canaan that is across the Jordan and onward is called the land of five nations, and that of Sihon and Og — two nations, Emori and Canaani — is the inheritance of the remainder, to include Keni and Kenizi and Kadmoni; and so he expounds in the passage of gifts that were said to Aharon (Numbers 18): ״therefore Levi shall not have״ etc. — to warn concerning Keni and Kenizi and Kadmoni. Furthermore, I found in the words of Rabbi Kalonymus that we thus read in the Sifrei: <b>And inheritance he shall not have.</b> These are the inheritance of five; <b>among his brothers</b> — these are the inheritance of seven: the inheritance of five tribes and the inheritance of seven tribes. And since Moshe and Yehoshua apportioned inheritance to only five tribes alone — for Moshe apportioned to Reuven and Gad and half the tribe of Menasheh, and Yehoshua apportioned to Yehudah and Efrayim and half the tribe of Menasheh — and the other seven took for themselves after the death of Yehoshua, therefore he mentioned five separately and seven separately."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:34.344079793Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}